{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -C 3 'Quote:|def _lines_english' src/hivemind/judging.py\nsed -n '184,295p' src/hivemind/model.py\nsed -n '168,193p' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\nrg -n 'D734|judging-v13|One next task' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\"","aggregated_output":"rg: src/hivemind/judging.py: IO error for operation on src/hivemind/judging.py: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ndef check_schema(value, schema, path='$', root=None):\n    \"\"\"A small validator for the subset of JSON Schema the prompts use: object/required/additionalProperties,\n    array/items/minItems/maxItems, string/enum/pattern, integer, number, boolean, null in anyOf, and $ref into the root's $defs.\"\"\"\n    root = root if root is not None else schema\n    if '$ref' in schema:\n        name = schema['$ref'].rsplit('/', 1)[1]\n        schema = root['$defs'][name]\n    kind = schema.get('type')\n    if 'anyOf' in schema:\n        # a value matching no option reports the closest options' errors (fewest), not merely the last option's\n        failures = []\n        for option in schema['anyOf']:\n            errors = check_schema(value, option, path, root)\n            if not errors:\n                return []\n            failures.append(errors)\n        fewest = min((len(errors) for errors in failures), default=0)\n        closest = list(dict.fromkeys(error for errors in failures if len(errors) == fewest for error in errors))\n        return closest or [f'{path}: matches no option']\n    if kind == 'object':\n        if not isinstance(value, dict):\n            return [f'{path}: expected object']\n        errors = []\n        for name in schema.get('required', []):\n            if name not in value:\n                errors.append(f'{path}.{name}: required')\n        properties = schema.get('properties', {})\n        for name, item in value.items():\n            if name in properties:\n                errors.extend(check_schema(item, properties[name], f'{path}.{name}', root))\n            elif schema.get('additionalProperties') is False:\n                errors.append(f'{path}.{name}: not allowed')\n        return errors\n    if kind == 'array':\n        if not isinstance(value, list):\n            return [f'{path}: expected array']\n        errors = []\n        if len(value) < schema.get('minItems', 0):\n            errors.append(f'{path}: fewer than {schema[\"minItems\"]} items')\n        if 'maxItems' in schema and len(value) > schema['maxItems']:\n            errors.append(f'{path}: more than {schema[\"maxItems\"]} items')\n        for index, item in enumerate(value):\n            errors.extend(check_schema(item, schema.get('items', {}), f'{path}[{index}]', root))\n        return errors\n    if kind == 'string':\n        if not isinstance(value, str):\n            return [f'{path}: expected string']\n        if 'enum' in schema and value not in schema['enum']:\n            return [f'{path}: {value!r} not in {schema[\"enum\"]}']\n        if 'pattern' in schema and not re.search(schema['pattern'], value):\n            return [f'{path}: {value!r} does not match {schema[\"pattern\"]}']\n        return []\n    if kind == 'integer':\n        return [] if isinstance(value, int) and not isinstance(value, bool) else [f'{path}: expected integer']\n    if kind == 'number':\n        return [] if isinstance(value, (int, float)) and not isinstance(value, bool) else [f'{path}: expected number']\n    if kind == 'boolean':\n        return [] if isinstance(value, bool) else [f'{path}: expected boolean']\n    if kind == 'null':\n        return [] if value is None else [f'{path}: expected null']\n    return []\n\n\ndef request_identity(request):\n    \"\"\"The exact serialized request and its archive key, shared by callers and validation.\"\"\"\n    encoded = json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)\n    return encoded, hashlib.sha256(encoded.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef call(archive, cfg, setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, purpose, *, transport=None):\n    provider = cfg.provider\n    request = build_request(setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, provider)\n    request_json, sha = request_identity(request)\n    hit = archive.lookup(sha)\n    prompt_chars = len(system) + len(user)\n    if hit:\n        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit\n        return Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n    started = time.time()\n    response = (transport or openai_transport)(provider, request)\n    seconds = round(time.time() - started, 1)\n    try:\n        content = response['choices'][0]['message']['content']\n        data = json.loads(content)\n    except (KeyError, IndexError, TypeError, json.JSONDecodeError) as error:\n        archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n                       request_sha256=sha + ':malformed:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n                       response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=None, prompt_chars=prompt_chars,\n                       input_tokens=0, output_tokens=0, cost_usd=0.0, seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n        raise SchemaError(f'malformed answer: {error}')\n    errors = check_schema(data, schema)\n    usage = response.get('usage') or {}\n    input_tokens = int(usage.get('prompt_tokens') or 0)\n    output_tokens = int(usage.get('completion_tokens') or 0)\n    cached_tokens = min(input_tokens, int((usage.get('prompt_tokens_details') or {}).get('cached_tokens') or 0))\n    price_in, price_out = PRICES.get(setting.model, (0.0, 0.0))\n    cost = round((input_tokens - cached_tokens) / 1e6 * price_in + cached_tokens / 1e6 * price_in * CACHED_INPUT_SHARE + output_tokens / 1e6 * price_out, 6)\n    call_id = archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n                             request_sha256=sha if not errors else sha + ':schema:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n                             response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False),\n                             prompt_chars=prompt_chars, input_tokens=input_tokens, output_tokens=output_tokens, cost_usd=cost,\n                             seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n    if errors:\n        raise SchemaError('; '.join(errors[:5]))\n    return Answer(data, call_id, sha, False, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost)\n## 7. Process (no drift)\n\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \"就测试一种，一次\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\").\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\n  sentence, in both directions.\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\n\n## 8. Steps and where we are\n\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n77:**Clean architecture Step 1 (2026-11-06, isolated work on `clean-arch`):** Alex reopened work with the clean architecture. An experimental prepared-source handoff now preserves the archived page, prior cleaned text, source-role decisions and selected-line mapping without changing the original database; quotations for prepared items must also occur contiguously in the original captured page. Two seven-item runs are available in the [clean architecture PRD](../clean-arch/PRD.md), one in the earlier selection order and one in recorded page-timestamp order. The source selector is not a production service and source ordering is not established event-arrival ordering. The runs expose unresolved semantic problems: citations can omit supporting facts despite an exact location match; model output can change a benchmark into a deployment, reverse a backup relation, omit a named customer or assign an unstated currency. A blinded 84-call check-placement/wording comparison and a 27-call same-article citation-completion diagnostic did not give a clean semantic fix and are not adopted. The latter missed an omitted connectivity condition and a reversed backup relationship, and left six expected evidence reviews unaddressed. A further five-round Codex–Claude council produced a narrowly scoped Step 1 link candidate, independently checked for prompt-contract drift. A six-article, 36-call blind comparison completed; the candidate still produced an explicitly self-contradictory link and both arms consistently omitted the same Kyber report and company response. It is not adopted and has not changed the active PRD prompt. A trace confirms that both the Kyber report and open Kyber thesis were supplied, and the raw model answers omitted the report and denial; the reason is not established. See ../poc/data/clean-step1-kyber-trace-2026-11-06/TRACE.md. An isolated six-call comparison showed that hiding the Kyber thesis did not recover the report or denial in any draw. A second six-call comparison returned them in 3/3 draws with the original Kyber paragraph alone and 0/3 with the full article; length, position and surrounding content changed together, so the reason is not isolated. Excerpt outputs have source-attribution limitations. Neither experiment changed state or established a production fix. (Superseded: the next task then was a whole-article coverage approach; the current next task is under \"One next task\".) See ../clean-arch/STEP1-IMPLEMENTATION-COUNCIL.md. The earlier four-round council agreed that no tested semantic fix is ready; its next investigation is a source-backed review of the 49-item historical run and its 160 evidence records, with overlapping issue flags and separate article-level omissions, then a separate comparison of the seven-item replays. See ../clean-arch/STEP1-COUNCIL-REVIEW.md. Preserve relevant evidence while identifying the next intervention; production/frozen history remains as described below. See [Step 1 run log](../clean-arch/STEP1-RUN-LOG.md) and [English reading page](../clean-arch/architecture.html).\n126:**Clean Step 1 source handoff council (2026-11-07):** The ongoing [council and offline checks](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-HANDOFF-COUNCIL.md) reconstructed 16 matching article-34 controls, all omitting a Kyber report and denial; the cause remains unknown. The 20-article saved source-role overlap review distinguished previously cited AI-generated summary lines and an unrelated recommendation from authored body. The clean runner does not send the saved source-role labels; the council chose to first compare original and previously selected source text on ten known articles. The isolated 60-call source-text comparison and condition-hidden review are complete; [results](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-TEXT-RESULTS.md) show specific contamination reductions alongside persistent omissions and changed meaning. It did not advance state or write production. The isolated six-article low-versus-medium source-fidelity diagnostic completed 36/36 calls and condition-hidden review. [Results](../clean-arch/STEP1-REASONING-FIDELITY-RESULTS.md) show partial improvements alongside persistent source-qualification and attribution concerns; no production setting is changed. The [prompt audit](../clean-arch/STEP1-FIDELITY-PROMPT-AUDIT.md) maps the observed failures to the full request and signed standard. The six-article isolated schema-description comparison completed 36/36 calls and condition-hidden review; the candidate did not preserve the repeated example qualification and is not adopted. [Results](../clean-arch/STEP1-SUMMARY-FIDELITY-RESULTS.md). A further six-article 36-call low-versus-medium comparison used corpus-cleaned sources outside the original 49-item clean replay and a fixed exploratory context; results were mixed, including unsupported links and incorrect attribution/date fields. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-ADDITIONAL-SOURCES-RESULTS.md). The structured-claims candidate was not sent after review revealed scope and complexity concerns. Council review of the next action is ongoing. The date-text schema-description diagnostic completed 48/48 calls on eight known cases, with mixed results; the candidate is not adopted. A selected-run census found twelve literal \"null\" strings in date-text fields, but no production writer impact is established. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-DATE-DESCRIPTION-RESULTS.md). A further preregistered eight-source date comparison completed 48/48 calls; the candidate lost a supported company-article statement date in all three draws on one source and is not adopted. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-DATE-NEW-SOURCES-RESULTS.md). A bounded corpus census confirmed 163 source pages across three explicit generated-summary structures whose labels were removed while some summary text was retained; two NVIDIA cases were reproduced through the cleaner. [Source provenance investigation](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-CENSUS.md). A read-only source-lineage replay reproduced 363/363 cleaned pages with current inputs, preserved ambiguous original-line locations, and surfaced the generated-summary label loss for review. [Source investigation and lineage replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-CENSUS.md). An offline neighboring-context observation exposed only 144 or 149 of 163 known labels and introduced many other page lines; it is not adopted as a general source fix. [Observations and viewer](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-CONTEXT-OBSERVATIONS.md). A new [saved-quote integrity investigation](../clean-arch/STEP1-QUOTE-INTEGRITY-CENSUS.md) reconstructed 360 saved answers across eight overlapping cohorts, including 78 prepared-source calls. Five saved unverified passage instances were complete matches under the existing normalization; an in-memory candidate recovered their original slices, while ten others remained unverified. The normalized source-slice lookup is now installed only in the isolated clean Step 1 runner; saved-answer and entry-point checks are recorded there. Page provenance, Unicode completeness, production resource budgets and writer integration remain open. The existing writer stores only one quote, whereas 63 of 160 evidence items in the 49-article exploratory trace have multiple passages. A [source-first 49-article coverage review](../clean-arch/STEP1-COVERAGE-CENSUS.md) separates material missing from the model input from source-visible omissions in the saved answers, with uncertain matter boundaries labeled. (Superseded: the next investigation then was why supplied material is missed; the current next task is under \"One next task\".) The canonical prompt and production configuration remain unchanged. Adding fallible role annotations remains a separate untested candidate. Council streams and handoffs are in `poc/data/clean-step1-ongoing-council-2026-11-07/`.\n159:## One next task\n448:**The one next task: finish judging-v13's repair to the council's line, then run the $0 blind test (D734, D735).**\n450:- **Alex chose the repair** (\"修一次再零成本盲测 (推荐)\", D734).\n459:The record before D734:\n470:- **The alternative** is to close judging-v13; poc-v118 stays the product.\n944:  numbers) was answered by him on 2026-11-15 (D505; see \"One next task\").\n946:  published rates); the current figure is in \"One next task\". (An earlier line here gave \"about $29.2\" as tracked spend; no decision or\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
