{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '448,474p' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\nrg -n 'def _lines_english|Quote:' src/hivemind\nrg -n 'range|shares|bridge|same_base|div-zero' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/gate.py | tail -n 55\"","aggregated_output":"**The one next task: finish judging-v13's repair to the council's line, then run the $0 blind test (D734, D735).**\n\n- **Alex chose the repair** (\"修一次再零成本盲测 (推荐)\", D734).\n- **The finish line (council rounds 49–50, D735):**\n  - at most two more review rounds: round 51 on the exact wording and cases (`REPAIR-DESIGN.md` v2), then one on the request the\n    harness actually sends and its checks;\n  - then the blind test once, as `REPAIR-DESIGN.md` §5 registers it;\n  - a serious issue left after the second round goes back to Alex.\n- **A clean blind test** returns to Alex as a request for the paid re-send.\n- **Nothing paid is sent before that.**\n\nThe record before D734:\n\n- **The paid gate stopped.** It was sent once at Alex's $0.50 ceiling (D732), and $0.3677 was spent. All 72 answers were refused by\n  the code checks, the 36 scored ones and the 36 diagnostic retries alike, so the joint arm is usable in 0 of 9 pairs.\n- **The cause is the format, not the judging.** The format's rules lived in `calc_check.py`, not in the request: the sent schema had\n  7 field descriptions. 0 of 90 member answers named a figure as the outcome. Under that layer, some checks refuse right answers.\n  The result does not answer D725's question.\n- **Council round 48 recommends** a bounded repair:\n  - each field's rule goes beside the field, with enums;\n  - the demonstrated check failures are fixed;\n  - then a registered $0 blind conformance test, after which a re-send of the same 36 requests is asked for.\n- **The alternative** is to close judging-v13; poc-v118 stays the product.\n- **Record:** `research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE-RESULT.md`. Nothing has been changed or sent since.\n\nEarlier in this line:\n- the $0 gate passed (council round 46ad);\nsrc/hivemind/views/judging.py:172:def _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes=(), hidden=0, full_dependencies=False):\nsrc/hivemind/views/judging.py:181:        lines.append(f'- {p[\"evidence_id\"]} [{p[\"tier\"]}; {p[\"speaker\"]}; original source {p[\"original_who\"]} {p[\"original_day\"]}; from {src.get(\"input_id\")} {src.get(\"publication_day\")}] {p[\"one_line\"]}\\n    Quote: {p[\"quote\"][:400]}')\n79:        comp('g3r', 'range_from_relative', ['g3', 'g3w'], (105.84, 110.16), 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), basis='guidance'),\n85:        comp('q4f', 'apply_growth', ['q3f', 'g12'], 127.1, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q4'), bridge='carry'),\n168:        ratio_extra['bridge'], prod_extra['bridge'] = 'br1', 'br2'\n223:    \"\"\"q01 and q02 with paired scenarios [46g.3]: low and high paths for the company total and the segment, each final range an estimate.\"\"\"\n231:        est('gfy', (400.0, 435.0), 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027'), 'the two paths, rounded', ['gfylo', 'gfyhi'], scenario='range'),\n239:            ['gdclo', 'gdchi', 'i106'], scenario='range'),\n266:            ['gfy28c', 'i256', 'i173'], scenario='range'),\n270:              'relations': [{'type': 'same_base', 'later': 'v22', 'earlier': 'v1'}], 'shared': [], 'compare_periods': []}\n309:         lambda r: ('C1' not in codes(r) and 'C8' in codes(r), 'passes C1, C8 without bridges'), '')\n311:         lambda r: (not r['errors'] and sum(x['type'] == 'bridge' for x in r['recorded']) == 2, 'bridges recorded, undetermined'), '')\n359:    r1x3 = r1('b')                                    # a point labelled range, read by the base\n360:    r1x3['figures'].append(est('altq3', 108.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), 'the guide as a point', ['g3'], scenario='range'))\n362:    item('R1bx3', R1_FAMILY, R